{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9ipWEL8ofsjQLGJuq2w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't do this review. The Bash sandbox won't start: both attempts failed with \"Sandbox is required but failed to initialize: Failed to create bridge sockets after 5 attempts. Restart to retry.\" Running outside the sandbox is disabled in this session, so no shell commands can run at all.\n\nThe brief says to name what's missing and stop if I can't get something I need. These are the things the sandbox failure blocks:\n\n- **Required tools:** `pose validate --strict`, `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp` and `pose artifact-check --spec pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation --strict`. A required tool must be run and passed before a draft can be accepted.\n- **Recommended tools:** the `assess` and `suggest review` commands.\n- **Inspecting the change and running tests:** `git diff 0482cbc2..804c6fd6`, `go test` and similar commands. I'd need those to judge the concurrency, correctness and requirements criteria with my own evidence.\n- **Final cleanup:** `go clean -cache` and removing leftover `go-build*` directories under `GOTMPDIR`. Both must run inside the sandbox. **Neither ran, so cleanup did not happen.** Since nothing was built or tested, there should be no leftovers, but that is not a completed cleanup, and the engine should treat this run as failed.\n\nI haven't written a `pose-draft` block. Without the required tools run and passed, POSE would refuse any draft, and approving or requesting changes without evidence would misstate what I checked. I haven't reported any defects for the same reason.\n\nTo retry, restart the session so the sandbox can set up again, then rerun the review. I made no changes to the repository."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":257,"cache_read_input_toke